-- title:
--   Exact Stieltjes running-record dividend mass on a half-open time interval
-- statement:
--   For a spectrally negative Lévy sample path, the actual dividend measure generated by its running supremum assigns to the left-open right-closed real-time interval (s,t] exactly the nonnegative right-limit increment rightLim(S∘toNNReal,t)−rightLim(S∘toNNReal,s). This follows from the globally monotone real-time Stieltjes witness already proved and Mathlib's precise Stieltjes interval formula, and holds without silently assuming ordinary right continuity or finite variation beyond the provided monotone running supremum. It is the exact measure increment used when replacing stopped discounted regulator integrals with discrete running-record partitions.
-- source:
